exercises.solution:
```python
from collections import Counter

def pullback(A, B, f, g):
    return [(a, b) for a in A for b in B if f[a] == g[b]]

def pullback_size(A, B, f, g):
    fa = Counter(f[a] for a in A)
    gb = Counter(g[b] for b in B)
    return sum(fa[c] * gb[c] for c in fa)
```

The pullback is the disjoint union, over $c \in C$, of the products of fibres $f^{-1}(c) \times g^{-1}(c)$ — which is why its size is $\sum_c |f^{-1}(c)|\,|g^{-1}(c)|$. When $C$ is a point, this is the product $A \times B$.
